        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugin-sdk): bound Anthropic Vertex ADC credential read",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\n`canReadAnthropicVertexAdc` in `src/plugin-sdk/anthropic-vertex-auth-presence.ts` reads the entire GCP ADC credentials file via unbounded `fs.readFileSync(credentialsPath, \"utf8\")` solely to check whether the file is readable — its contents are discarded. The path comes from `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` (an external, user-controlled env var) or the default gcloud ADC path, so a misconfigured or oversized file triggers an unbounded memory read just to report `true`.\r\n\r\nThe provider-local copy of this exact logic in `extensions/anthropic-vertex/region.ts` was already bounded with `tryReadSecretFileSync` + a 1 MiB limit in #109260 (\"reject oversized credential files in remaining readers\"). This standalone plugin-sdk preflight helper is a duplicate that sweep missed.\r\n\r\nThis PR mirrors the region.ts bound: replace the unbounded `readFileSync` with `tryReadSecretFileSync(..., { maxBytes: 1 MiB, rejectHardlinks: false })`, wrapped in `try/catch` (the helper throws `FsSafeError` on oversize) so an oversized credential file is rejected instead of slurped into memory. Presence-check semantics are unchanged for normal-sized files.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nProof script run with Node 22 + tsx (`hasAnthropicVertexAvailableAuth` against real temp files):\r\n\r\n```\r\nADC read bound: 1048576 bytes (1024 KiB)\r\n\r\n[1] Small ADC file (normal credential):\r\n    size:  32 bytes\r\n    NEW hasAnthropicVertexAvailableAuth: true  (expected true)\r\n\r\n[2] Oversized ADC file (2 MiB, exceeds bound):\r\n    size:  2097153 bytes\r\n    OLD unbounded readFileSync:           true  (read entire 2097153-byte file, returned true)\r\n    NEW hasAnthropicVertexAvailableAuth: false  (expected false: bound rejects oversize)\r\n\r\nRESULT: normal read preserved = true; oversized rejected by bound = true; old code read it fully = true\r\nPASS\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Normal-sized ADC file → still detected (`true`), no regression.\r\n- Oversized 2 MiB ADC file → rejected (`false`) by the 1 MiB bound; the old unbounded code read the entire file and returned `true`.\r\n- Existing unicode-path test still passes; preflight test still asserts no `existsSync` preflight; added a regression test for oversize rejection. \r\n",
        "branch": "fix/anthropic-vertex-auth-presence-adc-bound",
